---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Why Are My Breasts Spilling Out of My Bra? ('Quad-Boob') Fixes | BraSizeChecker"
  description="Fix breast spillage over top or side bra cups. Learn why small cup volume causes double-bust outlines and how sizing up cups eliminates quad-boob."
  canonical="https://brasizechecker.com/fit-guide/bra-spillage"
>
  <Header />
  <main class="flex-1 w-full max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 md:py-16">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[
      { label: 'Fit Guide', url: '/fit-guide' },
      { label: 'Breast Spillage' }
    ]} />

    <header class="mb-10 text-center sm:text-left">
      <span class="inline-block py-1 px-3 rounded-full bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-primary mb-3">
        Fit Diagnostic
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-4">
        Why Are My Breasts Spilling Out of My Bra?
      </h1>
      <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-body leading-relaxed max-w-3xl">
        Spillage—often creating a visible double-bust ridge ("quad-boob") under t-shirts—is a clear indicator that your bra cups are overloaded.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-body leading-relaxed text-sm sm:text-base">
      <!-- Quick Answer -->
      <section class="bg-canvas-soft-2 border-2 border-primary/30 rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-2">Quick Answer</h2>
        <p class="text-body leading-relaxed font-medium">
          Breasts spill over the top, sides, or underarms of a bra because <strong>the cup volume is too small</strong> to contain your breast tissue.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Possible Causes -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Plausible Causes</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">1. Cup Volume Is 1 to 2 Sizes Too Small</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">When cup depth is insufficient, breast tissue is forced up and out over the cup neckline or out the sides into underarm area.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2/60 border border-hairline rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-ink mb-1 text-sm">2. Wearing a Plunge Style on High-Volume Tops</h3>
            <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-body">Low-cut plunge bras have shorter center gores. Full-on-top breasts can spill inward toward the center seam.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- What to Check -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Practical Fit Checks</h2>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li><strong>T-shirt Test:</strong> Put on a snug fitted t-shirt over your bra. Look for a visible bump or line across your chest.</li>
          <li><strong>Underarm Check:</strong> Look under your arms for breast tissue being pinched out past the wire.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- What Size Change Might Help -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Recommended Size Adjustment</h2>
        <p class="mb-4">
          Keep your band size constant and increase your cup letter by one or two steps:
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 bg-canvas-soft-2 border border-hairline rounded-xl text-center mb-6">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold text-primary uppercase tracking-wider block mb-1">CUP INCREASE EXAMPLE</span>
          <p class="text-lg font-bold text-ink">If 34C causes spillage &rarr; Try a 34D or 34DD cup</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Calculator CTA -->
      <section class="bg-primary text-white rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 text-center sm:text-left flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center justify-between gap-6 shadow-md">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-white mb-1">Recalculate Your Bra Size</h2>
          <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-canvas-soft-2">Re-measure your bust loosely across the fullest point to find your baseline.</p>
        </div>
        <a href="/#calculator" class="flex-shrink-0 h-12 px-6 bg-surface hover:bg-canvas-soft-2 text-primary font-bold text-sm rounded-xl shadow-xs transition-colors flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>Calculate My Size &rarr;</span>
        </a>
      </section>

      <!-- Related Fit Guides -->
      <section class="bg-surface border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8">
        <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-bold text-ink mb-4">Related Fit Guides</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-3 text-xs sm:text-sm font-semibold">
          <a href="/fit-guide/bra-cup-gaping" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Why Do My Bra Cups Gap?</a>
          <a href="/fit-guide/underwire-digging" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Why Does My Bra Underwire Dig In?</a>
          <a href="/fit-guide/center-gore" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Why Doesn't My Center Gore Sit Flat?</a>
          <a href="/fit-guide" class="p-3 bg-canvas-soft-2 rounded-xl hover:text-primary transition-colors">&bull; Return to Fit Guide Hub</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
